    description: "Measured today on dev (69e541f119):\n\n  hypergumbo verify-claims . --claims docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml \\\n      --input <survey of this repo captured earlier today>\n      -> 18 INCONCLUSIVE (of 18 claim(s)), rc 2\n\n  (--input reuses a survey.json captured from this same tree at 01:23 rather\n  than re-running the ~9-minute self-analysis. The blocker reported below is a\n  language census over the repo's files, which that survey carries, so the\n  substitution does not affect the result — but it was a cached input and is\n  named as one rather than described as a clean run.)\n      -> every one for the same stated reason:\n         \"this repo contains code in language(s) with no taint catalogue\n          (bash, csharp, solidity), so the analysis could not look for the\n          flows this claim forbids. Absence of evidence here is not evidence\n          of absence.\"\n\nSo the self-proof currently establishes NOTHING. Not one of its 18 claims about\nhypergumbo's own filesystem / network / subprocess confinement resolves. It is\nnot returning a false all-clear — the gate is behaving correctly and saying so\nloudly, which is the good outcome of the honesty work — but the artifact the\nplan calls for (\"hypergumbo must USE its own io/DDG/CFG analysis to SHOW there\ncan be no exfiltration, as a machine-checkable artifact anyone can re-run\")\ndoes not currently show that.\n\nTHE BLOCKER IS NOT THE CLAIMS FILE. Its labels, zones, sources, sinks and the\nzone-barrier sanitizer all resolve correctly (verified while landing INV-todas:\nzero vocabulary errors across all 18). The blocker is that the repo contains\nbash, csharp and solidity files with no taint catalogue for those languages, and\nthe per-claim gate refuses to confirm anything while any such language is\npresent — regardless of whether those files could possibly participate in the\nflow a given claim forbids.\n\nTHAT LAST CLAUSE IS THE DESIGN QUESTION, and it should be settled before any\ncatalogue work: the gate is repo-scoped, not claim-scoped. A solidity fixture\nunder tests/ cannot reach cmd_sketch's filesystem writes, but it still blocks\n\"runtime-cli-no-host-fs\". Options, none costed yet:\n  (a) scope the language-coverage gate to languages REACHABLE from the claim's\n      declared sources rather than to languages PRESENT in the repo;\n  (b) catalogue the three languages (recall work, unbounded);\n  (c) exclude non-production / fixture paths from the language census, which\n      `is_test_file` / `classify_test_file` already know how to do and which\n      the boundary arm's production-default (WI-bifob) already does;\n  (d) accept it and state in SECURITY.md that the self-proof is inconclusive.\n(a) and (c) are the cheap ones and are not mutually exclusive. (d) is honest\nbut forfeits the plan's acceptance test.\n\nRELATED, DO NOT CONFLATE: INV-dabov is the BOUNDARY arm silently confirming for\na language with no io_primitives catalogue. This item is the TAINT arm doing\nthe opposite — refusing to confirm for the same class of gap. Both are about\nuncatalogued languages; one fails open and one fails closed, and fixing either\nshould not quietly change the other's behaviour.\n\nWI-vanun is adjacent and already filed: SECURITY.md asserts a verify-claims CI\ngate that does not exist (0 hits across 5 workflows). A gate wired today would\ngate on 18 inconclusive."  # f970
    fields:  # f970
      statement: "Running docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml against this repo must resolve its claims, or the self-proof the plan requires ('hypergumbo must USE its own io/DDG/CFG analysis to SHOW there can be no exfiltration, as a machine-checkable artifact anyone can re-run') does not exist. VIOLATED: all 18 claims return inconclusive, rc 2, every one because the repo contains bash / csharp / solidity files with no taint catalogue. The claims file itself is fine — its labels, zones, sources, sinks and zone-barrier sanitizer all resolve, verified with zero vocabulary errors while landing INV-todas."  # f970
      root_cause: "The language-coverage gate is REPO-scoped, not CLAIM-scoped: any language present anywhere in the tree with no taint catalogue blocks every claim, regardless of whether files in that language could participate in the flow a given claim forbids. A solidity fixture under a tests directory cannot reach cmd_sketch's filesystem writes, but it still blocks 'runtime-cli-no-host-fs'. Compounding it, the census counts non-production paths that the boundary arm's production-default (WI-bifob) already knows how to exclude."  # f970
